Command: U
Effect : undo commands
Modes  : x

Examples:
U   - undo last command
U 3 - undo last 3 commands

Note:  The commands that can be undone are the ones which actually change the
       file in some way.  These commands are: d, D, i, I, a, A, e, E, R, m, M, p,
       and P.  The 'O' command can be undone if there were no unsaved changes to
       the previous file.

       An undo cannot be undone.  Once you've undone something, it's undone for
       good.
